49. What happens if a Pod dies?

This is where Kubernetes' reconciliation model becomes powerful.

Suppose:

Desired = 3

Actual:
Pod A
Pod B
Pod C

Pod C crashes permanently:

Desired = 3
Actual = 2

Controller detects:

3 != 2

and creates a replacement.

Pod A
Pod B
Pod C ❌

      ↓

Pod A
Pod B
Pod D ✅

This is self-healing.

50. What happens if a Worker Node dies?

Suppose:

Worker 1 ❌

Pods on it disappear from the cluster's active capacity.

The control plane detects the node problem.

Depending on workload/controller and timing:

Worker 1
   ❌
   │
   ▼
Node unhealthy
   │
   ▼
Pods become unavailable
   │
   ▼
Controllers recreate workload
   │
   ▼
Scheduler
   │
   ▼
Worker 2 / Worker 3

Then new Pods can be scheduled onto healthy nodes.

